<p>Today Relay launched the <a href="https://relay.fm/designed">public and private feeds</a> of my new podcast, Designed in California. If you’re interested in the history of Apple, check it out. The first few episodes in the feed are episodes we previously released in the Upgrade podcast feed; our first all-new episode debuts next week.</p>
<p>If you’re a Kickstarter backer who pledged at a level where you’ll get the special member feeds, check your messages for information about how to redeem that pledge and get access to the special feeds.</p>
<p>And if you didn’t back the Kickstarter, you can now <a href="https://relay.fm/designed/join">join us via Relay</a> and get access to entire series of the show all at once, ad free. Next week, members will receive the <em>entirety</em> of our series about Apple’s mid-90s Mac OS crisis that led to the company buying NeXT and bringing back Steve Jobs, which led to the creation of Mac OS X. Those episodes will play out over the next six weeks in the main feed, but members will get all seven episodes, five hours and 15 minutes of content, all at once. (Plus the first of our monthly bonus episodes.)</p>
<p>There’s also a <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@designedinca">YouTube channel</a>, and Spotify users will find that video version available within Spotify as well.</p>
